  "body": "Adds an `indeterminate` property on the `HTMLProgressElement`\r\n\r\nresolves #2815 \r\n\r\nTo make the `<progress>` element more intuitive, I would like to add an `indeterminate` property. This property would be set to `true` initially and return true if no value attribute exists (for backwards compatibility) or if the `indeterminate` property is explicitly set to `true`.\r\n\r\nWhen the `value` attribute is changed the `indeterminate` property will be implicitly set to `false` (again for backwards compatibility). The `value` attribute will stay set if the `indeterminate` property is explicitly set to `true`.",
